            "<p><strong>Weight</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Definition</p>",
            "<p>Amount of matter in a body</p>",
            "<p>Force with which Earth attracts a body</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Formula</p>",
            "<p>m</p>",
            "<p>W = mg</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>SI Unit</p>",
            "<p>Kilogram (kg)</p>",
            "<p>Newton (N)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Nature</p>",
            "<p>Scalar Quantity</p>",
            "<p>Vector Quantity</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Dependence</p>",
            "<p>Constant everywhere</p>",
            "<p>Varies with gravity</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "jxfrhob",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "17. FRICTION (VERY DETAILED)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m4mplg0",
      "content": "Friction is the force opposing relative motion between two surfaces in contact."
    },
    {
      "id": "78pawkb",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>When It Acts</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Relative Magnitude</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Static Friction</p>",
            "<p>Before motion starts</p>",
            "<p>Maximum</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sliding Friction</p>",
            "<p>During sliding motion</p>",
            "<p>Less than static</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Rolling Friction</p>",
            "<p>During rolling motion</p>",
            "<p>Least</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Fluid Friction</p>",
            "<p>Motion in fluids</p>",
            "<p>Depends on speed &amp; shape</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dafibnr",
      "content": "Formula: Frictional Force (F) = μ × N"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fa52yhl",
      "content": "Where μ = Coefficient of friction, N = Normal reaction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g1hervl",
      "content": "μ has no unit (dimensionless quantity)."
    },
    {
      "id": "3nc2kym",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "18. IMPULSE-MOMENTUM THEOREM"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i0x4q9e",
      "content": "According to Newton’s Second Law, Force = Rate of change of momentum."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wj43jrs",
      "content": "F = (mv - mu) / t"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2i67asz",
      "content": "Multiplying both sides by t:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ld55r67",
      "content": "F × t = m(v - u)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vtsy4s8",
      "content": "Thus, Impulse = Change in Momentum"
    },
    {
      "id": "ezv4ykf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "19. TYPES OF COLLISION"
    },
    {
      "id": "uged3m2",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Momentum</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Kinetic Energy</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Elastic Collision</p>",
            "<p>Conserved</p>",
            "<p>Conserved</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Inelastic Collision</p>",
            "<p>Conserved</p>",
            "<p>Not conserved</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Perfectly Inelastic</p>",
            "<p>Conserved</p>",
            "<p>Maximum KE loss</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lltp03i",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "20. FORCE IN CIRCULAR MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cy158g9",
      "content": "Centripetal Force = mv² / r"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qkag4q8",
      "content": "Direction: Always towards centre of circle."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kdqumhk",
      "content": "If centripetal force is removed, body moves tangentially."
    },
    {
      "id": "m9yoe3t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "21. ADVANCED RRB EXAM POINTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gpo1roz",
      "content": "• Nuclear force is strongest force in nature."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zagwp1u",
      "content": "• Gravitational force is weakest fundamental force."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a9v3sm1",
      "content": "• Action and reaction act on different bodies simultaneously."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0alkfjv",
      "content": "• If net force = 0, momentum remains constant."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wr1pkpn",
      "content": "• Friction is self-adjusting up to limiting value."
    },
    {
      "id": "ewljv3l",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MCQs"
    },
    {
      "id": "q4lzyn6",
