    },
    {
      "id": "isk7tm9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q2."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1f0or5g",
      "content": "The momentum of a 20 kg body moving at 2 m/s is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "pjkasq8",
      "content": "A) 10 kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "wou0vot",
      "content": "B) 20 kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8rnsvzp",
      "content": "C) 40 kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "gfeflex",
      "content": "D) 80 kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f9txj80",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C (40 kg m/s)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1fqyggf",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "089z6gi",
      "content": "Step 1: Formula of momentum."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "yaz2zov",
      "content": "p = m × v"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4vjwz2t",
      "content": "Step 2: Substitute values."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hg9j35q",
      "content": "p = 20 × 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4b9feff",
      "content": "Step 3: Multiply."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "l2s9bwo",
      "content": "p = 40 kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nd4w5bh",
      "content": "Momentum is vector quantity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qh0skko",
      "content": "Final Answer = 40 kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "ua1k3ve",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q3."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ly3fapi",
      "content": "A force of 50 N acts on a body for 0.2 seconds. The impulse produced is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ffq1qw4",
      "content": "A) 5 Ns"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "sna8pbn",
      "content": "B) 10 Ns"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "caj8uqh",
      "content": "C) 20 Ns"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ovhzetj",
      "content": "D) 100 Ns"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "nmvwfcv",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: B (10 Ns)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6hex8c3",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "934ex3r",
      "content": "Step 1: Formula of impulse."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "h1o88pf",
      "content": "Impulse = Force × Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n41bc1y",
      "content": "Step 2: Substitute values."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "mhhiwgr",
      "content": "Impulse = 50 × 0.2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lvc0e5g",
      "content": "Step 3: Multiply."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "bg64y49",
      "content": "Impulse = 10 Ns"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "25fwr4i",
      "content": "Impulse equals change in momentum."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "h35x18c",
      "content": "Final Answer = 10 Ns"
    },
    {
      "id": "0oxi4ps",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q4."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ukms5k4",
      "content": "A 1 kg ball moving at 10 m/s collides with a wall and rebounds with velocity 6 m/s in opposite direction. Change in momentum is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "wkww4k6",
      "content": "A) 4 kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "gnsdzgb",
      "content": "B) 10 kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions comparing Mass vs Weight and their SI units frequently appear in RRB exams.",
        "Application of the Law of Conservation of Momentum in recoil of guns and rocket propulsion is a top numerical topic.",
        "Understanding Pseudo Force is essential for solving problems involving non-inertial frames of reference."
      ],
      "id": "jxx7msr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "y5iqi30",
      "content": "C) 16 kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "zrrso38",
      "content": "D) 20 kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d5w9dci",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C (16 kg m/s)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uf5px64",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "thtlymv",
      "content": "Step 1: Assign directions carefully."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h1ogbjf",
      "content": "Initial velocity (u) = +10 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iomqu88",
      "content": "Final velocity (v) = -6 m/s (opposite direction)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sbthjfb",
      "content": "Step 2: Formula of change in momentum."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "9p4cbrk",
      "content": "Δp = m(v - u)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fm8of59",
      "content": "Step 3: Substitute values."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ef266or",
      "content": "Δp = 1(-6 - 10)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "reaquxs",
      "content": "Δp = -16 kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4h0hwkx",
      "content": "Magnitude of change = 16 kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vcc6izg",
      "content": "Final Answer = 16 kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "hxj5qp9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q5."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yzpyfuc",
      "content": "A 5 kg block rests on a horizontal surface (g = 10 m/s²). If coefficient of friction is 0.4, frictional force is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hsvu3j8",
      "content": "A) 10 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "m0i3ror",
      "content": "B) 15 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4gdrmte",
      "content": "C) 20 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8xt9clz",
      "content": "D) 25 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "wy5akzk",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C (20 N)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8lqcbq2",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j34mghy",
      "content": "Step 1: Calculate Normal Reaction."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "utni357",
      "content": "N = mg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q5w667y",
      "content": "N = 5 × 10 = 50 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "onk3j3e",
      "content": "Step 2: Apply friction formula."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ddn5hmk",
      "content": "F = μ × N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "e50kcxe",
      "content": "F = 0.4 × 50"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l150o20",
      "content": "Step 3: Multiply."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "g5ymruf",
      "content": "F = 20 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "pgeqltj",
      "content": "Final Answer = 20 N"
    }
  ],
